<h1>Hardware Settings</h1>
<hr align="left" width="100.526%" size="5" class="whs3">
<p class="description"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Description:</b></span> <span class="Command">Hardware Settings</span> allows most of the settings in a profile to be saved and is used to achieve the best performance. Custom Settings allows the user to configure KUBE for a certain type of object and save those settings for future use. This command is accessible from the <span class="Path">System &gt; Hardware Settings</span> or by pressing the Hardware settings button on the toolbar</p>
<p>Hardware Settings window is divided in eight tabs related to different parts of the system and different stages of the scanning procedure.</p>
<ul>
<li style="margin-left:-20px;" class="kadov-p-CClick">
<p class="Click">&#160;Click on each Tab title to follow its description.</p>
</li>
</ul>
